{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to promise 90c57c85, NF-1, on the `time` pattern. Keep the\nlexical `TIME` pattern as it is in packages/bytes/src/ids.ts. Add no\nlookahead: a host can check a pattern with an engine that has none.\nThe description carries the rule that the pattern cannot: a whole\nsecond has no fraction. A value that ends in `.000Z` passes the schema\nand gets the server's refusal at the field path. The witness shows\nthat refusal.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}